body:
@Mopzilla Think of it as a specification rather than something to be fixed. Users need to understand the difference between Discrete and Continuous, what happens with Deterministic, and the implications of each combination.

However, indeed it is lacking sufficient documentation, so we plan to prepare some tutorial material.

Well, if we were to implement something besides documentation, I think we could add some helper functions like `AnimationMixer.reset()` and `AnimationPlayer.play_with_reset()` function that calls the reset in one line. Since we have revised the behavior of Discrete and Deterministic many times in the past and added some options for that, I believe there is almost nothing more we can support.
